WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.510
Heeyah! Heeyah!

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:32.900
Heeyah!

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.550
Oh, no!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.760
The beast is upon me!

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.370
- Quack
- (Shh.)

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.440
Greg, is there a beast out there?

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.680
Mmm...

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:46.930
I found a duck.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.440
Do you know how to make eggs from a duck?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.340
- I'm hungry.
- What about the beast?

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.220
The beast is upon me!

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.950
I didn't see any beast.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.530
That driver is nuts.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.500
Mmm, nuts.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.210
Whew! Well, that's good.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:00.860
Good?!

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.790
That crazy driver's taking us way off course!

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.710
- Really?
- Yeah!

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:08.060
Who knows where we are by now with that guy acting all bananas.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.800
Ooh, banana nut duck bread.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.970
- Whoa-ah!
- Whoa-ah!

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:17.430
Well, finally some good luck.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.220
Let's go to this creepy tavern and ask for some directions.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.060
But...

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.070
But it's creepy.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.100
Why don't you guys go ask for directions,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.660
and I'll just wait out... no, wait,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.300
I-I don't want to be out here by myself.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.040
How about you guys...

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.900
- Just go to the tavern!
- Okay!

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.320
- But you ask for directions.
- Fine, yeah, I'll do everything.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.410
I'm hungry.

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.340
- Go on!
- I-It's stuck.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.080
Oh!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.830
E-Excuse me, there.

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.880
Excuse me.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:51.960
Hmm?

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.160
You. Wait. Here.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.640
I'll get some food.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.640
Well, at least it has music.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.590
Well, hey, there, peach pot. Whatcha doing around...

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.190
Hey, what's that bird you got there?

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.960
It's a...
- I am Beatrice!

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.780
These two sweet kids and I got a bit lost in the...

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.690
Ah!

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.360
No birds allowed in my tavern!

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.610
No birds allowed in your...

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.730
It's a bad omen when a bluebird enters through your door.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.120
It's bad luck!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.620
Lady, bluebirds are good luck!

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.480
We bring joy and happiness to the...

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:27.000
Aah!

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.830
Good luck, bad luck... I don't need any of it!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.370
Curse you, lady! Curse you!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:32.870
You'll die someday, and I'll laugh... laugh!

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:33.910
Ha ha ha ha

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:34.480
Ohh!

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.040
Forget this. I'm out of here.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.170
Wirt, you get directions.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:38.020
W-Wait, no.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.020
- I-I don't want to...
- Just do it!

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.260
Who are you two anyway, bringing bad luck to my tavern?

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.850
I'm Wirt, and this is Gregory.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.180
And that's a horse!

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.940
That's great, but who are you?

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.170
I'm... Wirt.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.050
I'm... I'm just a-a guy, I-I guess.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:55.940
Um, w-what do you mean?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.220
- Well, he's the butcher...
- I'm the butcher.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.280
- ...the baker...
- Yeah!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.860
...the midwife...

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.620
...the master and apprentice...

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.780
the tailor.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.370
and I'm the tavern keeper.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.040
Who are you?!

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.290
I am hungry!

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.870
I-I-I don't know.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.380
I don't really like labels.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.290
I'm just sort of, like, myself, you know?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.550
Maybe he's simple?

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.840
No! Im just...

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.740
I'm just lost.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.280
See, w-we're trying to get to...

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.050
I'm the highwayman.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.470
Okay, good to know.
Well, so, you see...

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.920
♪ I'm the highwayman ♪

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.590
♪ I make ends meet ♪

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.400
♪ just like any man ♪

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.470
♪ I work with my hands ♪

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.020
♪ if you cross my path ♪

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.030
♪ I'll knock you out ♪

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.540
♪ Drag you off the road ♪

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:45.490
♪ steal your shoes from off your feet ♪

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.040
♪ I'm the highwayman ♪

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.040
♪ And I make ends mee-e-e-e-t ♪

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.550
Huuh, Hey.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.890
Are you wearing lipstick?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.520
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.730
Hmm? Who's out there?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.510
♪ Chop the wood to light the fire! ♪

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.190
What kind of person goes out chopping trees

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.410
♪ Tra-la-la-la! Tra-la-la-la! ♪

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.520
in the middle of a thunderstorm at night?

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.420
♪ Tis it much that I require! ♪

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.620
What kind of a person talks to a horse?

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:23.390
♪ When the fog of life surrounds you, ♪

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.990
♪ When you think you've... ♪

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:25.990
Ooh Ah.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.500
Hmm.

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.170
- Excuse me?
- Huh?

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.170
I was wondering if you knew the way...

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.550
uh, I mean, I-I'm...

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.800
- her name is Adelaide, and...
- Oh, it's a girl you're after, eh?

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.550
No! I-I mean, yes, but...

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.480
Oh, ha ha.You're not the witless,

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.560
simple-minded fool everybody takes you for.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.170
Everyone thinks I'm...

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.050
You're the young lover.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.290
What? Young lover? No, uh...

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.200
If you really want to get with this Adelaide gal...

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.200
I-I don't. I-I mean, I-I ...

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.360
well, here's what you do.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.940
♪ Write a loving letter, boy ♪

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.540
♪ that swoops and sweeps and curls ♪

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.200
♪ The calligrapher is just the thing to help you win your girl ♪

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.170
♪ then you'll need to dress up smart ♪

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.690
♪ the tailor's here by chance ♪

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.250
♪ He'll stitch your trousers, hole your belt ♪

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:11.790
♪ in the fine couture of France ♪

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.570
♪ your shoes, my goodness, how they're worn, ♪

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.210
♪ but you're too young to know ♪

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.290
♪ Nothing courts a woman's scorn more than scuffs on the toe ♪

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.880
♪ The cobbler can attend to that ♪

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.460
♪ Meanwhile, you must have cake ♪

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:24.380
♪ The baker and patissier need work for goodness sake ♪

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.390
♪ high, dee, diddly, um-de-dum-de-day ♪

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.550
♪ What a merry time we'll have upon your wedding day ♪

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.100
- What?
- ♪ High, dee, diddly, ♪

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.140
♪ um-de-dum-de-day ♪

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.230
♪ there's work for all when little boys get married ♪

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:37.120
No, no, no, no.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.850
Y-You guys, I-I-I'm not getting married.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.650
I'm just trying to find...

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.230
♪ That pointy cone upon your head ♪

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.070
- ♪ You can't be wearing that ♪
- Oh, no, please.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.070
♪ The milliner, he’ll fix you up ♪

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.070
♪ with a proper high silk hat  ♪

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.050
♪ The bride, of course, she’ll need a dress ♪

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.910
Mm.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.950
If I have to be outside, then those jokers do, too.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.620
Oh, hey, Beatrice! Do you want some food, too?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.840
No. How's Wirt doing getting directions?

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:58.370
Mm, pretty good.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.080
♪ Hi, dee, diddly, um-de-dum-de-day ♪

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.170
♪ What a merry time we'll have ♪

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.410
♪ upon your wedding day! ♪

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.000
ouh...

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.670
What about that woodsman?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.340
I bet he knows these woods better than anybody, huh?

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.880
All right, horse, good riddance!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.400
nee-hehehe

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.640
Lover! Lover!

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:18.360
No, y-you guys,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.440
Adelaide isn't... I-I'm just...

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.440
Young lover, sing us your love song!

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.110
Love song?

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.030
Yeah, lover! Sing us your love song!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.030
- No, I-I-I don't have a...

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.030
Sing, lover, sing!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.200
No...

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.770
Sing, lover, sing!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.070
Midwife, no!

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.680
Sing, lover, sing!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.860
Aah! Oof.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.450
Sing, lover, sing!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.110
Sing, lover, sing!

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.260
Sing! Boy, sing!

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.790
Oooh...

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.710
♪ My name is Wirt,
and his name is Greg ♪

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.540
♪ We're related 'cause my mom remarried ♪

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.960
♪ and then gave birth to him with my stepdad ♪

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.880
♪ We're not from around here ♪

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.890
♪ can you all give me ♪

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.120
♪ Some directions today? ♪

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.070
♪ So we can be on our ♪

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.480
♪ wa-a-a-y ♪

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.000
This ain't no love song.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.000
It's a metaphor.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.400
Keep it together, tailor.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.080
Hey!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.280
Uh, yes?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.380
I know what you are!

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.240
You're a pilgrim!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.400
What? What, like the...

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.240
the guys who eat turkey and cranberry sauce?

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.160
- No, you're a pilgrim!
- A pilgrim?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.410
You're a traveler on a sacred journey.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.500
You're the master of your own destiny.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.920
The hero of your own story!

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.170
A pilgrim.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:23.600
Tell us your feats, pilgrim!

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:27.340
- What other challenges have you...
- Regale us with your travels, pilgrim!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.260
One time, Wirt fell on a gorilla.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.300
And helped me find this frog.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.930
- More! Tell us more!
- Tell us more!

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.100
- Let the cat out of the bag!
- We want to hear it!

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.100
And, oh, uh, I met this helpful woodsman

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.100
who told us which direction to go to avoid

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.190
The Beast!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.860
- Huh!
- The beast.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.440
Oh, you guys have heard of the beast, too?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.200
We all know The Beast, pilgrim.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:55.490
♪ He lurks out there in the Unknown ♪

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.700
♪ seeking those who are far from home ♪

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.220
♪ hoping never to let you return ♪

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.880
♪ ooh-ooh, better beware ♪

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.300
♪ ooh-ooh, the beast is out there ♪

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:17.300
♪ ooh-ooh, better be wise and don't believe his lies ♪

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.710
♪ For once your will begins to spoil ♪

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.770
♪ he'll turn you to a tree of oil ♪

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:27.980
♪ and use you in his lantern for to burn ♪

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.590
Wait, wait, wait! Lantern?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.490
The woodsman was the guy with the weird lantern, not the beast.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:38.580
Pilgrim, he who carries the dark lantern must be the beast.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.340
What? No, the woodsman's a good guy.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.520
He warned us of the beast

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.500
and told us which direction to go to avoid him.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.000
And now you're more lost than ever, huh?

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.500
Yeah, but...

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.440
Oh, yeah.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.100
hey, can you give us some directions?

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.860
Our friend Beatrice is trying to take us to

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.390
Adelaide of the pasture, the good woman of the woods.

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:55.680
She can help us get home.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.680
You don't need directions, pilgrim.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.430
You follow that compass inside your heart.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.080
Uh, No, I think we need directions.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:03.680
Ahhh!

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.520
Beatrice!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:07.770
Go save your friend and get yourself home!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.770
- Pilgrim!
- You got it!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.650
Uh... Okay.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:14.990
Never say die, never say die!

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:18.570
Oh, boy, I guess I'm really doing this.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.730
Horse, I'm just gonna pretend like I can ride you, all right?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.080
Beatrice!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.920
Beatrice?

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.920
Another one of those trees.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:34.840
Halt!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:35.840
It's you!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:36.930
Hey, Mr. Woodsman!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.060
I told you to leave these woods!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:40.850
Beatrice!

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.850
You're turning her into an edelwood tree!

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.520
You were the beast all along!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.020
Huh?!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.690
Whoa!

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:51.610
What is this?

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.030
Greg, get Beatrice!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.080
What are you doing?!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:56.860
Boys,

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.200
the beast is upon you!

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.030
Agh!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:02.700
Oh!

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.380
ugh.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.540
Beatrice, you all right?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.270
Yeah, I just...

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.670
I saw a weird shadow

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.220
and then stupidly flew into a tree and got knocked out.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.220
Oh, well, we're all right now.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:19.520
Wirt was amazing!

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.320
He sang a song, rode a horse, and saved you from the axe guy!

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:24.640
He's the pilgrim!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:25.910
That's all well and good,

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:28.140
but you were supposed to get directions.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:28.660
I did.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.060
We just got directions from Fred before you woke up.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:31.730
Who?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.230
Oh, uh, Beatrice, meet Fred the horse.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.650
Nice to horse your acquaintance.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.780
You can talk?!

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.990
It seems you're running out of oil, Woodsman.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.290
Why not let me take the lantern for awhile?

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:47.710
Begone, beast!

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:51.790
I've fought you for the lantern before, and I'll fight you again!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.040
No need for violence, woodsman,

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.910
Now, what direction did those children go?

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:58.380
Now, what direction did those children go?

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.220
Now, what direction did those children go?

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.680
Now, what direction did those children go?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.390
You leave those children be!

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.180
Ah ha ha ha ha ha!

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:08.180
Beast...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.890
Beast!

